---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Art from '../components/Art.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Data with a human story">
  <section class="hero home-hero split">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">DATA ANALYST · CREATIVE VISUALISER · SOCIAL RESEARCHER</p><h1>Making data<br /><em>meaningful.</em><br />Making ideas visible.</h1><p class="lead">I’m Monalisa. I connect evidence with human experience—through thoughtful analysis, creative visuals, and a curiosity about what makes our world work.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`${base}visualisation/`}>Explore my work <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${base}about/`}>A little about me →</a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-art"><Art /><span class="handwritten">There’s a story in every pattern.</span></div>
  </section>
  <section><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A FEW WAYS I SEE THE WORLD</p><h2>Where curiosity<br />becomes <em>work.</em></h2></div><p>From railway delays to community participation, I’m drawn to questions that matter to people.</p></div>
    <div class="grid portfolio-grid"><a class="work-card" href={`${base}visualisation/`}><span class="index">01 / SEE THE PATTERNS</span><h3>Data<br />Visualisation <span>↗</span></h3><p>Creative Tableau stories that turn complex information into something you can explore.</p><span class="tag">Tableau · Visual storytelling</span></a><a class="work-card" href={`${base}analytics/`}><span class="index">02 / ASK BETTER QUESTIONS</span><h3>Data<br />Analytics <span>↗</span></h3><p>Notebooks, social research, and policy analysis with evidence at their heart.</p><span class="tag">Python · Research · Analysis</span></a><a class="work-card" href={`${base}ceg/`}><span class="index">03 / CONNECT WITH PEOPLE</span><h3>Civic<br />Engagement <span>↗</span></h3><p>An outreach experiment bringing flyer design and analytical thinking together.</p><span class="tag">Design · Experiment · Community</span></a><a class="work-card woodworking-card" href={`${base}woodworking/`}><span class="index">04 / MAKE ROOM FOR IDEAS</span><h3>Creative<br />Woodworking <span>↗</span></h3><p>Self-taught furniture design and inventive storage solutions, built through repurposing, prototyping, and iteration.</p><span class="tag">Design-build · Resourcefulness · Craft</span></a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="feature split"><div><p class="eyebrow">FEATURED CASE STUDY / ARLINGTON, MASSACHUSETTS</p><h2>A small flyer.<br />A bigger <em>question.</em></h2><p class="lead">Can creative outreach help more neighbours find their voice in community life?</p><p>Explore the Civic Engagement Group experiment: from an invitation to participate, to the patterns in website visits across three outreach phases.</p><a class="button" href={`${base}ceg/`}>Follow the experiment ↗</a></div><a class="feature-image" href={`${base}ceg/`}><img src={`${base}images/ceg/phase1-before-after.webp`} alt="Spring 2025 outreach chart comparing website activity before and after the campaign" loading="lazy" width="1416" height="483" /><span>DESIGN + DATA + COMMUNITY</span></a></section>
  <section class="intro-note"><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE PORTFOLIO</p><h2>A researcher’s mind.<br /><em>A maker’s imagination.</em></h2><p>My work brings together 7+ years in impact-driven NGOs, social policy research, and a self-directed journey into data and design. Whether I’m exploring a dataset or building a piece of furniture, I learn by questioning, making, and refining.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}about/`}>Meet Monalisa →</a></section>
</Layout>
